formulas.latex:
\begin{aligned}
					&\text{The line }y=mx+n\text{ is an oblique asymptote, it exists only if}\\
					&\text{ there is no horizontal asymptote.}\\
					&m=\lim_{x\to \pm \infty}\frac{f(x)}{x}\text{ (the slope of the asymptote)}\\
					&n=\lim_{x\to \pm \infty}(f(x)-mx)
					\end{aligned}

